    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1-a8">

                <pb facs="0113" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg5"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 6 in No.
                    351.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Count Welsersheimb to
                        Mr. Grant.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the esteemed favor of January
                    30, No. 160, and in pursuance of the note of January 20, 1893, the imperial and
                    royal ministry of foreign affairs has the honor of informing the honorable envoy
                    of the United States that the state attorney at Pisek has withdrawn, on March 18
                    last, his charge against Edward Drucker for violation of paragraph 45 of the law
                    of April 11, 1889, No. 41, after it has been shown by the naturalization
                    certificate of Edward Drucker that he has acquired American citizenship in due
                    form.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welsersheimb</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">For the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
